<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Motion Transfer and Generation</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show more motion transfer results on Sprites in <a href="#A2.F6" title="In Appendix B Additional Results ‣ Bitrate-Controlled Diffusion for Disentangling Motion and Content in Video" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A6</span></a>. Following previous methods, we also quantitatively assess disentanglement quality by measuring the attribute accuracy of videos generated by our model, using the pre-trained video classification network from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>. <a href="#A2.T4" title="In B.1 Motion Transfer and Generation ‣ Appendix B Additional Results ‣ Bitrate-Controlled Diffusion for Disentangling Motion and Content in Video" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A4</span></a> reports the motion and content accuracy for each attribute category, demonstrating that our method produces correct disentanglement results and achieves state-of-the-art performance on par with C-DSVAE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table A4</span>: </span><span id="A2.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Cross-driven attributes accuracies(%) of different methods on Sprites test set. “Action” represents the motion attribute and the others are content attributes.</span></figcaption>
